# Deliberate binary breaks in 1.10.0, relative to 1.9.0. See the release note in README.md.
#
# Migrating to Visitor 1.8.0 generalised the traversal entry points over the journal's element
# type: dfs, bfs and dfsAll on Traversable, Graph, AbstractGraph and VertexMap now read
#
#   def dfs[E, J <: Appendable[E, J]](visitor: Visitor[V, E, J], ...)(using random: Random)
#
# in place of the old form, which fixed the journal to (V, Option[R]) and took a using
# Evaluable[V, R]. Dropping that Evaluable is what breaks binary compatibility: it changes the
# erased signature. The earlier, purely generic rewrite (Visitor[V, R, J] ->
# Visitor[V, Mapped[V, R], J]) did NOT, since Mapped is an alias for the same tuple and type
# parameters erase - which is why PR #63 passed MiMa and PR #64 did not.
#
# The Evaluable was already dead: these methods only forward to Traversal, which no longer
# takes one. Keeping it would have preserved compatibility at the cost of a permanently unused
# parameter in the public API, and would have left SimpleVisitor and ParentedVisitor unusable
# through every Gryphon traversal entry point.
#
# Under PVP, 1.9.x -> 1.10.0 is a major bump, so these breaks are permitted. This file retires
# itself: once previousRelease moves past 1.9.0, MiMa stops consulting it.
#
# The lines below are MiMa's own suggestions from the failing run, not hand-written.

ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.AbstractGraph.bfs$default$5(com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Visitor,java.lang.Object,scala.Function1)scala.util.Random")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.AbstractGraph.bfs(com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Visitor,java.lang.Object,scala.Function1,com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Evaluable,scala.util.Random)com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Visitor")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.gryphon.core.AbstractGraph.dfs$default$5(com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Visitor,com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.DfsOrder,java.lang.Object)scala.util.Random")
